  {
   "id": "switching-test",
   "title": "Switching test circuit",
   "page": 7,
   "description": "The circuit the switching times are measured in. A 5 V pulse generator with 50 Ω output and edges of 0.01 µs or faster drives the LED through RE, with C across RE. The detector runs from 5 V, decoupled by 0.1 µF at the supply pin, and its open-collector output is pulled up to 5 V by RL = 270 Ω. ton and toff run from the input's 50% point to the output's edge; tf and tr are the output's own fall and rise.",
   "parts": [
    {
     "ref": "U1",
     "type": "ic",
